        MONOCHROME -- VER, the monster of MONOCHROME (Pt 2), in DOORS (with its creator's permission)

            loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bonellocristian78-lab/Gradish-Mode/claude/sei-qui-con-noi-ye4k62/Monochrome"))()

        VER comes out at the next door: it stands in the doorway, the lights go out around it, its joints crack, and it
        wakes. Then it hunts you, as in its game: it hears you move, it sees you (less in the dark: a light in your hand
        gives you away), it walks, it runs when it sees you -- or it freezes, silent, a bait, and then bursts at you. Hide
        in a wardrobe if it spotted you, and hope it throws it off. It has the lights: it cuts them, they flicker as it
        passes. Lose it and it gives up and goes; get ahead of it and it comes back out of the dark at the next door.

        All of VER as its game has it (its kit, Monochrome.rbxm: the model out of the place, with its bones):
          - its walk: MonsterGait, its own procedural gait -- legs on IK, the step, the bob, the lean, its arms, its head
            turning to you, idle breathing; walk to run; the bait pose; the grab; the strobe twitch. No animation assets:
            its game has none, it moves its bones itself (so nothing needs uploading, and it moves in DOORS too)
          - its sounds: its double footsteps, its presence (the loop, louder the nearer it is, silent as a bait), the
            crack of its grab, the static of its strobe, its detonation, its hitches, its joints
          - the camera shaking as it comes near (its own noise shake), the film grain, the game's grade
          - its kill: the grab (its pose, the cracks, the strobe), its face filling your screen, every other sound gone,
            its scream, the snap, black; and its phantom scares
          - the lights: its blackouts (the lamps go down one by one, clicking, and come back: dim, the room still seen)
            and their flicker
          - a radar, in DOORS' hotbar (and on R): its dial on your screen, its sweep, a blip, a ping and its distance

        Three more of it, before the loadstring (else VER as its game has it):
            _G.VER = "White"    -- white, black-eyed; its blackouts are whiteouts; its face on white
            _G.VER = "Glitch"   -- made of DOORS' Glitch: its purple, its cubes; it skips ahead; near you, its cubes on your screen
            _G.VER = "Noise"    -- a TV above the next door (Noise's): hold its prompt, MONOCHROME's tape plays on it, the
                                   screen bursts and VER crawls out of it as Noise does (Noise's Emerge); then it walks as VER

        Its body, horns and eyes are its creator's: if Roblox will not load them here, it takes its own shape out of its saved
        place (its body and horns as its game's physics hold them, VERBody.lua), on its bones, moving as they move (the console,
        F9, says which). With its model put on Roblox for all by its creator: _G.VERModel = its id, and its mesh itself.

        Only you see it (the server does not know it is there). getgenv().__Monochrome() takes it away.
]]

